# Compiled binaries
/bin/

# SQLite database files.
#
# The -wal and -shm files are created by WAL journalling mode: -wal holds
# committed-but-not-yet-checkpointed transactions, -shm is a shared-memory
# index into it. Both are transient and must never be committed — a .db without
# its matching -wal can be missing recent writes.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Test and coverage output
*.out
coverage.html

# Environment files (these hold SMTP credentials)
.env
.envrc

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea/
# .vscode is ignored wholesale except for the two files that are project
# config rather than personal preference: the extension recommendations, and
# settings that mirror mise.toml (golangci-lint as the linter, -race on tests,
# and the toolsManagement guard that stops the Go extension installing its own
# copies of the CLIs pinned in [tools]).
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
*.swp
/questions.md